From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: set the content protection regions for msm8998

Measured on a Pixel 2 XL: TZ refuses the resume outright.

  qcom-venus cc00000.video-codec: venus: scm_set_remote_state(resume=1) = -22
  qcom-venus cc00000.video-codec: venus: scm_set_remote_state(resume=0) = 0

venus_set_hw_state() maps that -EINVAL to success, so nothing reports it and
the venus CPU is never released. Everything downstream of that follows: the
first VBIF write in venus_set_registers(), 0x00000003 to base+0x80124, never
returns and takes the NoC with it, and with the preset table skipped the
firmware never answers so venus_boot_core() times out with -110. Releasing the
CPU by hand instead (venus_reset_cpu()) does not help -- the wrapper registers
it writes are equally unreachable.

The missing step is earlier. venus_boot() only calls
qcom_scm_mem_protect_video_var() when res->cp_size is set, and msm8998_res sets
none of the cp_* fields, so the content protection regions are never programmed
into TZ.

The values come from the downstream context banks exactly as the porting note
in venus_boot() describes: cp_size is venus_ns/virtual-addr-pool[0] and the
nonpixel pair is venus_sec_non_pixel/virtual-addr-pool, which msm8998-vidc.dtsi
gives as <0x70800000 0x6f800000> and <0x1000000 0x24800000>. As a cross-check,
sdm845 independently carries the same four values, and the venus_ns IOMMU
stream list downstream matches mainline's msm8998 venus node exactly.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index 8f0b70a77d67..7a3b16b621ac 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -868,6 +868,25 @@ static const struct venus_resources msm8998_res = {
 	.vmem_id = VIDC_RESOURCE_NONE,
 	.vmem_size = 0,
 	.vmem_addr = 0,
+	/*
+	 * Without these venus_boot() skips qcom_scm_mem_protect_video_var(), TZ
+	 * then refuses qcom_scm_set_remote_state(resume) with -EINVAL -- which
+	 * venus_set_hw_state() maps to success -- and the venus CPU is never
+	 * released. The whole subsystem stays dark: the first VBIF write in
+	 * venus_set_registers() (0x80124) takes the NoC down, and with the
+	 * presets skipped the firmware never answers and boot_core times out.
+	 *
+	 * Taken from the downstream context banks, per the porting note in
+	 * venus_boot(): cp_size is venus_ns/virtual-addr-pool[0] and the
+	 * nonpixel pair is venus_sec_non_pixel/virtual-addr-pool, which in
+	 * msm8998-vidc.dtsi are <0x70800000 0x6f800000> and
+	 * <0x1000000 0x24800000>. sdm845 independently carries the same four
+	 * values.
+	 */
+	.cp_start = 0,
+	.cp_size = 0x70800000,
+	.cp_nonpixel_start = 0x1000000,
+	.cp_nonpixel_size = 0x24800000,
 	.dma_mask = 0xddc00000 - 1,
 	.fwname = "qcom/venus-4.4/venus.mbn",
 };
